        <ul class="text-xs text-slate-900 space-y-1.5 pl-4 list-disc font-medium leading-relaxed">
          <li><strong>Distributed Systems:</strong> Multiple independent computers talking over a network to act like one unified system while handling partial crashes.</li>
          <li><strong>Hardware Design:</strong> Connected clusters of standard machines are cheaper and scale further than building one giant shared-memory computer.</li>
          <li><strong>Software Model:</strong> Standard operating systems with a helper Middleware layer on top is the modern industry standard.</li>
          <li><strong>Cloud Computing:</strong> Renting computing power on demand with automatic elasticity and pay-as-you-go billing.</li>
          <li><strong>Shared Responsibility:</strong> Cloud providers protect the physical datacenters; you are always responsible for securing your own data and user passwords.</li>
        </ul>
